import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Retro — cached fixpoint + the enablement floor, measured","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/enablement-floor.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/enablement-floor.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/enablement-floor.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-cached-fixpoint-the-enablement-floor-measured" tabindex="-1">Retro — cached fixpoint + the enablement floor, measured <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-cached-fixpoint-the-enablement-floor-measured" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — cached fixpoint + the enablement floor, measured”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-10-19. <strong>Follows</strong>: <code>fixpoint-api-and-conv-sweep.md</code> (its two open items). <strong>Commits</strong>: <code>02e05f9</code> (rulecache knobs + payload-internal parents), <code>ca42c16</code> (guard transport for stored composites), this commit (probe + retro + GOALS).</p><h2 id="item-1-—-synthesize-rules-cached-takes-the-fixpoint-api" tabindex="-1">Item 1 — <code>synthesize_rules_cached</code> takes the fixpoint API <a class="header-anchor" href="#item-1-—-synthesize-rules-cached-takes-the-fixpoint-api" aria-label="Permalink to “Item 1 — synthesize_rules_cached takes the fixpoint API”">​</a></h2><p><code>rounds</code> / <code>max_emitted</code> / <code>on_round</code> now pass through <code>synthesize_rules_cached</code> into <code>meta.synthesize_rules</code>, and both scalar knobs join <code>cache_key</code>&#39;s <code>params</code> — a <code>rounds=3</code> mint is a different problem instance from <code>rounds=1</code> and must not collide. <code>on_round</code> is a callable: it enters the key through its <code>_hook_sig</code> proxy (source text when inspectable, else module+qualname) — a <em>vetoing</em> observer truncates the fixpoint, so sharing the unobserved entry would be a wrong hit; an uninspectable signature degrades to a miss. Documented hit semantics: the observer reports <strong>live rounds only</strong> — a warm load calls nothing.</p><p>Also landed, from the same retro&#39;s &quot;unbuilt&quot; list: <code>RuleCache.load</code> resolves parents <em>payload-internally</em> — records decode in stored order and each decoded rule joins the resolver, so a round-≥2 composite whose parent is itself a <code>syn_*</code> mint round-trips self-contained (emission order guarantees parents precede dependents; all-or-nothing miss semantics unchanged).</p><p>Tests (<code>tests/test_rulecache.py</code> §e, 4 tests): cached <code>rounds=3</code> returns the fixpoint strata under a monkeypatched-exploding synthesizer; <code>rounds=1</code>/<code>rounds=3</code>/<code>max_emitted=2</code> are distinct entries; the observer fires on cold mints only and a vetoing callable keys separately; a guarded <code>syn_*</code>-parented composite reloads its guard from the payload.</p><h2 id="item-2-—-the-enablement-floor-measured" tabindex="-1">Item 2 — the enablement floor, measured <a class="header-anchor" href="#item-2-—-the-enablement-floor-measured" aria-label="Permalink to “Item 2 — the enablement floor, measured”">​</a></h2><p>The named blocker is <strong>fixed</strong>: guard transport for stored composites. <code>store_object</code> writes the minted rule&#39;s <code>guard_pats</code> + <code>parents</code> as a <code>&quot;guard&quot;</code> record field (the <code>rulecache</code> binding wire form — additive; older readers ignore it); <code>admit_object</code> resolves the named parents as rows of the same store <em>transitively</em> and re-runs <code>meta._compose_guards</code>. <code>missing_hooks</code>/<code>serializable</code> keep their meaning (what the bare record rebuilds); admit annotates the record with <code>&quot;transported&quot;</code>, and <code>full-data</code> counts missing-minus-transported. A parent that rebuilt weaker than it declared refuses the transport — composing over it would smuggle a weakened guard. 5 tests in <code>tests/test_discovery_gauntlet.py</code> cover spec-write, restore+fire, transitivity, the honest partial admit, and the gate.</p><h3 id="the-premise-pay-measurement-lab-probes-conv-fold-premise-pay-probe-py" tabindex="-1">The premise-pay measurement (<code>lab/probes/conv_fold_premise_pay_probe.py</code>) <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-premise-pay-measurement-lab-probes-conv-fold-premise-pay-probe-py" aria-label="Permalink to “The premise-pay measurement (lab/probes/conv_fold_premise_pay_probe.py)”">​</a></h3><p>The conv+BN fold composite mints in 4 rounds (974 emitted), premise closure = 8 rules (<code>batch_norm_expand</code> + 4 <code>conv_channel_*</code> anchors + 3 syn intermediates). Stored, admitted — <code>transported=[&#39;check&#39;,&#39;derive&#39;]</code> — and measured on the real eval-mode <code>ConvBN</code> site:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>stage</th><th>measured</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>transport</td><td>hooks rebuilt transitively; composite fires on the seed</td></tr><tr><td>truth (real region)</td><td>accepted=1, <strong>1eq/0ne</strong> — fp64-equal on the real site</td></tr><tr><td>truth (premise-anchored)</td><td><code>verify_law(seed, folded, ALL_RULES+closure)</code>: <strong>derivable, replayable, 2-step cert</strong> (<code>conv_channel_shift_sp</code> + the depth-3 syn composite); under <code>ALL_RULES</code> alone: not derivable</td></tr><tr><td><strong>pay</strong></td><td><code>fires=1</code>, typed=1, ill=0, verified=<code>same</code> — and <strong>changed=False</strong>: extraction kept the spelled term (<code>spelled=34874.3</code> vs <code>fused=34874.337</code>)</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>The dependent mint does not pay in extraction.</strong> The composite&#39;s fused member exists in the e-class but <code>dag_cost</code> prices its RHS&#39;s spelled weight-fold trees (<code>mul</code>/<code>reshape</code>/<code>rsqrt</code>/<code>add</code> over the bound params) as real ops — the constant-fold win materializes only at <em>lowering</em> (<code>IRModule._fold_weight_chains</code>), a layer the term-level cost model cannot see. The premise-of-admitted-composite accounting is now implemented and ran; the pay leg is measured <strong>false</strong>, not assumed.</p><p>Caveat on the formal floor: the full <code>run_gauntlet</code> on the composite did not terminate in <code>pl.measure</code> on this box (&gt;9 min even on a one-case corpus — the 83-rule <code>_reach</code>/derivability saturation is a scaling gap, separate from starvation). The per-stage numbers above are the bounded measurement.</p><h3 id="verdicts-per-family" tabindex="-1">Verdicts per family <a class="header-anchor" href="#verdicts-per-family" aria-label="Permalink to “Verdicts per family”">​</a></h3><ul><li><strong>conv anchors in the closure</strong> (<code>conv_channel_shift_sub_sp</code>, <code>conv_channel_scale_sp</code>, <code>conv_channel_scale_l_sp</code>, <code>conv_channel_shift_sp</code>) + <strong><code>batch_norm_expand</code></strong>: <strong>enabled-but-opt-in</strong> — a dependent mint exists, fires, and truth-verifies (real region + premise-anchored replayable cert), but pays nothing in extraction → the floor&#39;s pay leg fails → <strong>not DEFAULT</strong>. Enablement (the mint exists at all) is real; pay is the measured refusal.</li><li><strong>the other 56 CONV_FOLD_RULES</strong>: named refusal — truth-starved AND no paying dependent mint measured.</li><li><strong>the composite itself</strong>: now storable/admittable via transport and premise-derivable, but does not pay → not a DEFAULT candidate.</li><li><strong>BATCH_NORM_RULES</strong> (the other arities): unchanged — <code>fires=0</code> variants have no dependent mint; <code>batch_norm_expand</code> shares the closure&#39;s account.</li></ul><h2 id="what-stays-open" tabindex="-1">What stays open <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-stays-open" aria-label="Permalink to “What stays open”">​</a></h2><ul><li>The corner-reaching truth route (enumeration vocabulary for <code>conv2d</code>/channel-views, or witness-driven sites) — requirement #1 still stands; the premise-anchored <code>verify_law</code> replay is the honest partial substitute measured here.</li><li><code>run_gauntlet</code>/<code>pl.measure</code> on guarded minted composites does not terminate within the box — the reach/derivability saturation needs a bounded budget for composite-scale rules.</li><li>A cost model that credits compile-time weight folds (the fused member&#39;s spelled weight trees are free after <code>_fold_weight_chains</code>) would flip the measured pay leg — that is a <em>cost-model</em> gap, not a law-truth gap.</li></ul><p><code>DEFAULT</code> unchanged. Gate account: ruff/format/ty clean on touched files; <code>tests/test_rulecache{,_codec}.py</code>, <code>test_meta_fixpoint.py</code>, <code>tests/test_discovery_{gauntlet,evidence}.py</code> all pass (34 + 58 + 44; the standalone <code>test_rulecache</code> fp64 tests still need the suite&#39;s torch-import order — pre-existing at HEAD, verified).</p>`,18)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};